# Formatting

- Indent with 8 spaces
- Do not wrap lines to 80 or 100 characters. Keep statements on one line unless a break is required for syntax or readability of a long chained expression
- Print width is effectively unlimited (Prettier `printWidth: 999`)
- Blank line before `return` when another statement precedes it
- Blank line after `if` / `for` / `while` / `switch` / `try` blocks
- Blank line after a `const` / `let` / `var` group when the next statement is not another declaration
- Adjacent declarations stay together; do not insert blank lines between them
- Do not pad the inside of braces (no blank line right after `{` or right before `}`)
